{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:8637d2579a61284c","name":"Colossal Vehicles","source":{"id":"source:reference-8637d2579a61284c","title":"Colossal Vehicles","revision":19857,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:44:38Z","sha256":"e2520c1c241df39f2d6b6d955a1e7bcc4e9a5c755b704762202b398d04078862","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19857","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Colossal%20Vehicles&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-8637d2579a61284c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal Vehicles function as individual combatants in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"},". For example, the heroes might be in command of an ",{"tag":"a","children":["LAAT/i Gunship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/LAAT/i_Gunship","referenceId":"reference:4ec307279de7b7a7"},", flying over the battlefield, dropping off or picking up ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," and manning the guns to both devastate enemy forces and to deal with antivehicle ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Emplacements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Emplacements","referenceId":"reference:edfd22971bb42275"},". However, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["LAAT/i Gunship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/LAAT/i_Gunship","referenceId":"reference:4ec307279de7b7a7"}," acts as an individual combatant, meaning it doesn't gain the benefit of taking half the damage from all non-",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attacks"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Frigate) and larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," do not usually participate directly in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"},". However, including a grounded ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," as a piece of terrain can produce interesting tactical choices. For the most part, Colossal (Frigate) and larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," have difficulty targeting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," are treated as Gargantuan for the purposes of being targeted by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," weapons (thus, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," take a -20 penalty on attack rolls against ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Having a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," act as terrain (blocking particular avenues for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},") can produce situations where tactical decisions must be made, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," weapons can also be used to target ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," on the battlefield, effectively serving as antivehicle ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Batteries"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Batteries"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Orbital Bombardment"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Combatants in a ground battle can be devastated by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," in orbit above the planet. As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commander"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commander","referenceId":"reference:16af7be312e1840b"}," of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," can order a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"}," to aim at  single square on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," battlefield. The square is considered to be at Long ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},", and the ship must make an attack roll against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10 to hit the target square. If successful, all ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," in that square take normal damage for that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon System"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_System"},", or half damage on a miss. That ship cannot make any other attacks until the beginning of the Commander's next turn.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Orbital Bombardment should be used by the Gamemaster only as a means of making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," encounter more dangerous. A single shot from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"}," weapon is usually more than enough to destroy a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"},", so Orbital Bombardment should not be used lightly. Orbital Bombardment should occur only if the needs of the adventure require it rather than as a means for resolving combat.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
